Root cause

The primary synthetic journey JSON is mandatory and was moved successfully.
The next command uses the optional glob
`synthetic-journeys.json.*` as though at least one companion were mandatory.
With no matching file and Bash `nullglob` disabled, the literal pattern is
passed to `mv`, which returns non-zero and activates the fail-closed rollback.

Classification

OPTIONAL_EVIDENCE_GLOB_FALSE_REQUIRED

Bounded correction

- Keep the primary `synthetic-journeys.json` move mandatory.
- Move zero or more companion files through an explicit bounded loop that
  skips the unmatched literal pattern and uses `mv --` for each real file.
- Do not suppress errors for companion files that actually exist.
- Add isolated shell-contract tests for zero, one and multiple companions.
- Keep backup verification and postdeploy checksum generation unchanged.
- Publish the new immutable r4 freeze only after full local tests, review,
  merge-commit and post-merge CI are GREEN.

Backup and retry contract

- Preserve both r2 and r3 backups and tags unchanged.
- The authorized R15.2 retry requires another fresh timestamped root-owned
  mode-0700 backup and may run exactly once after the source release is GREEN.
- The archived pre-r3 epoch, failed r3 epoch and all technical evidence remain
  append-only; no cleanup or reclassification is allowed.
- The existing terminal-epoch rearm is required again before the R15.2 Canary.

Unchanged boundaries

- Maximum ten REAL SFW Canary sessions and a 24-hour bounded epoch.
- At least five valid REAL samples plus GREEN technical SLO before promotion.
- UNKNOWN provenance fails closed; human acceptance remains DEFERRED.
- Adult media, AVS, payment, external publishing, controlled beta and
  production remain CLOSED.
